# The zero tokens of a run `take` hands out (zero_run, their one caller,
# pinned by huge::tests::zero_axioms_called_from_zero_run_only): kernel
# zero-fill facts under the allocator's rules.
# The fresh pages: zero_run's requires tie the premise to the mark, which
# only `take` raises, so what is left is mmap(2)'s zero fill of a private
# anonymous mapping that nothing has written since.
axiom_fresh_anon_zero	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
# The Purged pages: the premise that Huge::rediscard succeeded for the
# run's pages (purge::purged_is_zero read true) is challoc's own and not
# checked (a follow-up takes purge::purged_zero's PurgedZero witness, as
# the class claim path does).
axiom_discarded_zero	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# write_zero: Verus checks its requires at every caller (split_guard, from
# Huge::prepare); its body, the write, is trusted.
write_zero	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	RefinedRust	trusted (requires, checked at every caller: the huge lock held, `held_by`, the byte committed, `vspec::unbacked::committed`, the byte in the region apart from every live run's guard, `spares_guards`, and the byte in no live run, `apart_from_runs`; not checked: that the byte is still read-write, as `committed` never expires, which below the mark in guard-install mode rests on `Huge::mixed_guards` being set whenever a `PROT_NONE` page outside a live run's guard may exist)
